1. Introduction:
This project contains the implementations of the `head` and `wc` utilities in C. The utilities allow you to display the beginning of a file and count lines, words, and bytes.


2. Compilation and Execution:
To compile the utilities, open your terminal and navigate to the project directory. Then, follow these steps:

Compile the Programs:
Use the `make` command to compile the `head` and `wc` utilities:

Run the program:
./head [-n number] [files...]
./wc [-clw] [files...]

3.Cleaning the Project
To remove object code and executables, you can use the `make clean` command

